 Data Licence is UNCHECKED.","credit_line":"Coastline: geoBoundaries (CC BY 4.0), from URA Master Plan 2014 - captured 14 Sep 2026, orientation only","lineage":"geoBoundaries metadata, quoted verbatim: boundarySource 'Urban Redevelopment Authority, derived from ADM 3', licenseSource 'https//data.gov.sg/dataset/master-plan-2014-subzone-boundary-no-sea', boundaryYear 2016, sourceDataUpdateDate Thu Jan 19 07:31:04 2023, buildDate Jul 05, 2023, meanAreaSqKM 724.2749814174942.","transform":"Exterior rings only (the source has NO interior rings - asserted at write time, so a lake could not be drawn as land); a duplicated closing point dropped because the renderer closes with Z; rings sorted by area, largest first; coordinates ROUNDED TO 5 DECIMAL PLACES, maximum displacement 0.76 m. No simplification: the source's own simplified release is already small, and a second lossy pass is one more thing to re-verify at every future use.","area_sq_km_total":722.91,"area_sq_km_by_ring":[637.29,29.86,28.68,10.09,4.7,3.27,2.18,2.05,1.5,1.18,1.1,1.02],"note":"A MIRROR IS EVIDENCE ABOUT A CAPTURE, NOT ABOUT A SOURCE. Fetched from GitHub on 14 Sep 2026, pinned to the commit and checksum above, because the egress proxy blocks data.gov.sg, naturalearthdata.com and overpass-api.de. URA's own publication was never read here. VINTAGE: MP2014 lineage. Total drawn land is 722.91 sq km against roughly 735 today, so the outline is about 12 sq km short of the current coast; the westernmost drawn point is 103.6054 E, which is short of Tuas Port, and no GitHub-reachable source checked on 14 Sep contains Tuas Port either. Orientation only, never a survey boundary. WHAT IT REPLACED: a 40-point Natural Earth hull that left 7 of the 348 schools outside the land it drew. This one contains 348 of 348, and pipeline/audit_integrity.py checks that, and checks these counts against this file, on every run. SHAPE: 12 rings, 653 points. Ring 0 is the main island and holds ALL 348 schools; the other 11 hold none. They are mostly islands - Tekong, Jurong Island, Ubin, Sentosa - but not all: one is the City Terminals port land, which the source maps as a polygon detached from the mainland."}